{"name":"Pink Perennial","hex":"#c034af","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"perennial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lasting or remaining active throughout the year, for multiple years, or all the time.","Continuing without cessation or intermission for several years, or for an undetermined or infinite period; never-ending or never failing; perpetual, unceasing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant that is active throughout the year, or has a life cycle of more than two growing seasons.","A thing that lasts forever.\nA person or thing (such as a problem) that appears or returns regularly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perennial"}],"entries":[{"title":"Perennial","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, the term perennial is used to differentiate a plant from shorter-lived annuals and biennials. It has thus been defined as a plant that lives more than 2 years. The term is also loosely used to distinguish plants with little or no woody growth from trees and shrubs, which are also technically perennials. An estimated 94% of plant species are perennials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Cykoria_podroznik_pokroj.jpg/330px-Cykoria_podroznik_pokroj.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perennial","wikidata":"Q157957"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/RIMG0163uf.JPG/500px-RIMG0163uf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/RIMG0163uf.JPG/1280px-RIMG0163uf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/RIMG0163uf.JPG/500px-RIMG0163uf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dahlia plants are tender perennials that originate from climates that are warm all year round and need special care to survive cold winters.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARIMG0163uf.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Switchgrass_roots.jpg/500px-Switchgrass_roots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Switchgrass_roots.jpg/1280px-Switchgrass_roots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Switchgrass_roots.jpg/500px-Switchgrass_roots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Switchgrass is a deep-rooted perennial. These roots are more than 3 meters long.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwitchgrass_roots.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=